Step 1: Run Your Web App
sudo systemctl start apache2

Access:

http://localhost/login.php
🦈 Step 2: Capture Traffic Using tcpdump
sudo tcpdump -i any port 80 -A

👉 Now submit login form

You will see something like:

POST /login.php HTTP/1.1
username=admin&password=1234

✔️ This proves:

Password is visible in plaintext
HTTP is insecure
🦈 Step 3: Using Wireshark (GUI)
Open Wireshark
Select interface

Filter:

http
Submit login form
Click packet → Follow → HTTP Stream

👉 You’ll clearly see credentials

🔐 Fix It

Enable HTTPS:

sudo a2enmod ssl
sudo a2ensite default-ssl
sudo systemctl restart apache2

Now test again:

https://localhost

👉 In Wireshark:

You’ll see TLS encrypted data
No readable password ✅

